{"t": 1794118438.9977553, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}, {"content": "from catalog.pager import page\n\n\ndef test_first_page_is_page_one():\n    items = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    assert page(items, 1, 2) == [1, 2]\n\n\ndef test_subsequent_pages():\n    items = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    assert page(items, 2, 2) == [3, 4]\n    assert page(items, 3, 2) == [5]\n\n\ndef test_page_past_the_end_is_empty():\n    assert page([1, 2, 3], 5, 2) == []\n", "path": "tests/test_pager.py"}], "message": "Fix page() to use 1-based page numbers (fixes #57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794118442.4823751, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated `number` as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page even though the API documents `?page=1` as the first page.\n\n- Compute the slice offset as `(number - 1) * size`.\n- Add tests covering the first page, later pages, and pages past the end.\n\nFixes #57.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `python -m pytest -q` \u2192 3 passed", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in catalog.pager.page (fixes #57)"}, "ok": true}
